  nodePositions: []
  nodeAbstract: 
  nodeTextLayers:
  - title: What is zinc's role in the insulin vesicle?
    basic: "Zinc is needed for insulin to form hexamers. \nRising zinc concentration
      in the vesicle leads to the formation of more hexamers."
    intermediate: 
    advanced: "Two zinc ions are required for each insulin hexamer. \nEach zinc ion
      is coordinated by three histidine residues from three separate insulin molecules.
      \nThis coordination provides the structural stability of the hexamer."
  nodeSpriteLayer: []
